From 4ff7983e56983e2964badc8e02abe40beda0c104 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pooya Parsa <pooya@pi0.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:43:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kthread: add park points for architectures that cannot keep a
 stack

An architecture whose kernel stacks live outside guest memory (arch/wasm:
each task runs on its own Wasm stack in the host engine) cannot save a
sleeping task's continuation. To bring the whole machine state into
memory, for a snapshot or to move a task, it parks every task at a point
where nothing on the task's stack is needed again, and later resumes it on
a fresh stack.

Add linux/kw_park.h and a kw_park_point(fn, arg) in the main loop of each
kernel thread that a minimal system runs: kthreadd, kthread workers,
workqueue workers and rescuers, smpboot threads, devtmpfsd, oom_reaper,
kcompactd, kswapd, khvcd, kjournald2 and ext4lazyinit. Each sits where the
thread holds no locks and has no wait queue entry or timer on its stack.
fn(arg) re-enters the loop; kthreadd, kcompactd, kswapd, devtmpfsd and
kjournald2 get a separate loop function so that their one-time setup is
not redone. Waits that a wakeup does not end (wait_event*()) also end
while kw_park_pending(), and kcompactd, kswapd and kjournald2 then skip
their work and go back to the park point.

Without CONFIG_KW_PARK both helpers are empty inlines.
